# Excludes these paths from the Netlify deploy bundle entirely (same
# .gitignore-style syntax, applied before the publish directory is
# selected - works regardless of whether one is set, and this repo
# doesn't set one: everything at the repo root gets published as-is,
# since there's no build step (see CLAUDE.md)). Without this file,
# Netlify deploys the *whole* repo, which meant every one of these was
# directly fetchable with real content at
# https://trac-studio-staging.netlify.app/<path> - confirmed live
# during a 2026-09-11 pentest: the complete DB schema + every RLS
# policy (schema.sql, supabase/*.sql), Edge Function source including
# mint-coa's exact validation/rate-limit logic (supabase/functions/),
# this project's own internal docs and security-incident history
# (CLAUDE.md, replit.md), the product proposal, the smart contract
# source, and the separate C2PA service's source.
#
# The app itself only ever references (verified via a grep of every
# src=/href= in index.html/app.html/collector.html): the three HTML
# files, supabase-config.js, legal-content.js, fonts/*.woff2, and
# assets/hero-gallery.jpg - everything below is unreferenced by the
# live app, on top of being sensitive/internal.
*.sql
*.md
server.py
.replit
/supabase/
/docs/
/contracts/
/c2pa-signing-service/
/attached_assets/

